On the way to my first successful Wizard ascencion (neu-hum-wiz), at
one point I stopped at a polytrap to internalize some intrinsics. So I
took off the armor item that I started with (and other layers
underneath) and stepped onto the trap. No effect. Hunh? Oh, right, I
was also carrying the Quest item for Wizards. Put that in a bag and
tried again. No effect. What? Tried again and again. Checked
inventory. Oh, right, I was wielding the artifact weapon that Wizards
get when they're rewarded for a sacrifice. Geez, with this class it
takes effort to *not* be magic-protected! Triple redundancy!

I had tried and failed with a few other wizards due to running into
soldier ants and the like, but this time I found a WoW in an early
store, chose boots of knocking and SDSM, and with a nice low AC and
reflection, the rest was easy. Getting Frost Brand was a plus but I
coulda done it with just the above-mentioned weapon. I don't think I
went under 1/3 max HP for the rest of the game. I botched putting one
bag into another for a magical explosion; lost some food and other
replacables, replaced it by polypiling (with lotsa my usual input
magical tool).

